WEBVTT

00:00:06.967 --> 00:00:10.377
We will save a room record in a temporary file, then

00:00:10.377 --> 00:00:13.262
recover its seat count, price and open flag.

00:00:13.262 --> 00:00:16.540
The goal is to make the writer and reader agree on

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:18.442
what each stored value means.

00:00:46.067 --> 00:00:49.438
A byte stream moves a sequence of bytes, small units

00:00:49.438 --> 00:00:52.421
of stored data, without treating them as text.

00:00:52.421 --> 00:00:54.560
Files opens that byte connection.

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:57.932
DataOutputStream adds typed binary output: it writes

00:00:57.932 --> 00:01:00.395
each value according to its Java type.

00:01:00.395 --> 00:01:03.896
Our binary record schema is the agreed field types and

00:01:03.896 --> 00:01:07.203
order: an int count, a double price, then a boolean

00:01:07.203 --> 00:01:07.527
flag.

00:01:07.527 --> 00:01:10.963
These writes store values without field names or type

00:01:10.963 --> 00:01:11.417
labels.

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:15.072
Typed binary input uses DataInputStream to interpret

00:01:15.072 --> 00:01:15.843
those bytes.

00:01:15.843 --> 00:01:19.249
Each read must match the corresponding write in type,

00:01:19.249 --> 00:01:20.406
order and meaning.

00:01:20.406 --> 00:01:23.876
Swapping two fields of the same type can silently give

00:01:23.876 --> 00:01:25.161
them wrong meanings.

00:01:25.161 --> 00:01:28.503
Try with resources closes each stream, including its

00:01:28.503 --> 00:01:29.531
file connection.

00:01:29.531 --> 00:01:32.873
The writer closes before reading begins, and finally

00:01:32.873 --> 00:01:34.608
removes the temporary file.

00:01:34.608 --> 00:01:37.950
An incomplete record ends before a required field is

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:38.657
fully read.

00:01:38.657 --> 00:01:41.806
EOFException reports that unexpected end of file.

00:01:41.806 --> 00:01:44.055
It does not supply a default value.

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:46.214
Predict the three printed lines.

00:01:46.214 --> 00:01:49.260
Match each read to its write, then follow which

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:50.880
variable each print uses.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.565
Pause here before running.

00:01:57.483 --> 00:02:00.850
The reader recovers four seats, a price of two point

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:02.404
five, and true for open.

00:02:02.404 --> 00:02:05.835
The matching reads interpret the stored values in the

00:02:05.835 --> 00:02:06.677
agreed order.

00:02:06.677 --> 00:02:09.979
The streams close and the temporary file is deleted

00:02:09.979 --> 00:02:11.533
after this complete run.

00:02:11.856 --> 00:02:14.985
Change only the written price, then predict which

00:02:14.985 --> 00:02:16.326
printed line changes.

00:02:16.326 --> 00:02:18.688
Next, remove the final boolean write.

00:02:18.688 --> 00:02:21.817
Which read would fail, and why should the program

00:02:21.817 --> 00:02:25.073
report an incomplete record instead of treating the

00:02:25.073 --> 00:02:26.031
room as closed?
